Our changes to Wine Mono 9.4.0 (all MIT, as Mono's class libraries are),
built by ../build-wine-mono.sh into the tarball the Makefile pins:

wine-mono-0001-ndp4-installpath.patch
    The support MSI also writes NDP\v4\Client and \Full InstallPath (both
    registry views). SQL Server Compact 3.5 SP2's installer edits
    [InstallPath]\CONFIG\machine.config and stopped with 1603 without them.

wine-mono-0002-assemblyfolders-v3.patch
    The support MSI also writes .NETFramework\AssemblyFolders\v3.0 and
    \v3.5 (both views), as .NET 3.5 SP1 leaves them: Meedio's setup took
    their absence for .NET 3.5 missing and ran Microsoft's 3.5 SP1 setup,
    which refuses on Windows 10 ("Turn Windows features on or off").

wine-mono-0003-netfx35-feature-files.patch (sg10)
    The support MSI leaves what a machine with the .NET Framework 3.5
    feature on has: NDP\v3.5 InstallPath and CBS, NDP\v2.0.50727/v3.0 CBS,
    NDP\v3.0\Setup\Windows Presentation/Communication Foundation
    InstallSuccess+Version, AssemblyFolders\DX_1.0.2902.0 (Managed DirectX,
    which Mono implements; MeediOS's setup ran DirectX's setup without it),
    the 64-bit view's AssemblyFolders in [ProgramFiles64Folder]; files:
    Framework(64)\v3.5\csc.exe (3.5's compiler: the 2.0 runtime with the 3.5
    libraries) and Program Files (both views)\Reference Assemblies\
    Microsoft\Framework\v3.0 and v3.5 with Mono's 2.0-api reference
    assemblies (System.Core 3.5, System.Xml.Linq, System.ServiceModel...),
    where AssemblyFolders points. build-msi-tables.sh: a top-level
    ProgramFilesFolder/ProgramFiles64Folder in the image is the MSI's own
    folder of that name. Existing prefixes get it through sg-session's
    sg_mono_support_refresh (0.1.0-109), which re-applies the support MSI
    when it changed -- Wine does not while the version stays 9.4.0.

mono-0001-sg-fixes.patch
    System.Core: System.Diagnostics.Eventing.Reader (EventLogWatcher,
      EventLogSession, EventLogReader...), our own; there are no event logs
      to read, but programs that name the types load (athenaNet Device
      Manager's service and tray program).
    WineMono.Security: X509Store Import/Remove/Clear through crypt32 (were
      NotImplementedException): X509Store.Add/Remove reach the system store.
    System: X509Store.Certificates is a new collection each call, as .NET's
      (Remove while enumerating: "Collection was modified").
    System.Configuration: a section the runtime ignores (<startup>) may
      appear twice in a .config, as .NET allows.
    corlib: Environment.UserInteractive is false in a window station that is
      not visible (a service's), as .NET decides it (was always true: a .NET
      service that runs as a console program when interactive stopped).

mono-0002-system-drawing-framework-names.patch,
corefx-0001-brush-nativebrush.patch
    System.Drawing: the private names .NET Framework's System.Drawing has and
      programs reach by reflection -- Graphics.nativeGraphics, Pen.nativePen,
      Brush.nativeBrush (fields), GraphicsPath(IntPtr, int),
      Bitmap.FromGDIplus(IntPtr) -- over the same GDI+ handles. GdPicture
      (AmbirScan's imaging library) failed in its type initializer, and
      AmbirScan with it (David 2026-10-02). Mono's own code keeps
      nativeObject, a property now for Graphics and Pen.

mono-0003-settings-declared-late-and-wmi-event-watchers.patch (sg11)
    System: ApplicationSettingsBase reads a setting a program declares at
      run time (Properties.Add) from the user.config that already has it.
      The provider had loaded the file's value under an untyped property
      of its own; once declared, that value was read through it, could not
      be deserialized and came back null -- DYMO Connect ended on every
      start after its first (XDocument.Parse(null), David 2026-10-05).
    System.Management: an event query's sink needs no stub between
      apartments (WMI runs in the process); ManagementEventWatcher.Start
      threw PlatformNotSupportedException (GetDemultiplexedStub_f), which
      ended DYMO Connect's launcher at every sign-in.

test/mono-fork-test.sh checks each.

wpf-0001-pts-managed-engine.patch
    PresentationFramework: PTS, the engine WPF's flow layout hands pages,
      columns and paragraphs to, in managed code (MS/Internal/PtsHost/
      PtsEngine.cs, our own, written from the interface's declarations in
      Pts.cs and how PtsHost uses them). Wine Mono's PresentationNative has
      no PTS: FlowDocument, RichTextBox, FlowDocumentScrollViewer and
      FlowDocumentReader stopped with EntryPointNotFoundException
      (CreateInstalledObjectsInfo) -- Sonos Desktop Controller among them
      (David 2026-10-02). Paragraphs stack down columns, text breaks into
      lines through the client's FormatLine, containers and subpages lay
      out their own children, finite pages break between columns and
      pages, lists, sections and BlockUIContainer are placed, tables laid
      out row by row (row spans, row heights, breaks between rows),
      floaters and figures in text put at their side (a figure where its
      anchors say) with the lines beside them narrowed (sg8; before, they
      were not drawn). Not yet: text on both sides of one, column
      balancing, repeated table headers, footnotes. PtsCache:
      without Line Services there is no penalty module (optimal
      paragraphs off).

wpf-0002-managed-textformatter.patch
    PresentationCore, Wine Mono's managed TextFormatter (FullTextLine):
      TextHeight, TextBaseline, MarkerHeight/Baseline, DependentLength and
      IsTruncated answered (were NotImplementedException; flow documents
      ask for them); a list item's marker (bullet, number) is drawn; an
      inline object (InlineUIContainer) is measured while its line is
      formatted, not again when drawn or queried (the flow layout can only
      measure it then: InvalidCastException); the paragraph's alignment
      (centre, right) is applied -- centred text drew at the left; a
      line's break is searched with each run shaped once (prefix widths
      summed; the search shaped every prefix again -- 2.8 ms a line in a
      flow document, now well under 1); a right-to-left paragraph's lines
      start at the right, and its carets and bounds are counted from there
      (right-to-left text drew at the left, under the element's mirror).

wpf-0003-composite-font-fallbacks.patch
    PresentationCore's composite fonts (Global User Interface, Sans Serif,
      Serif, Monospace): every family map's Target ends with families a
      Stained Glass OS machine has -- Liberation, DejaVu, Noto CJK,
      Symbola. They named only Windows' (Segoe UI, Tahoma, MS Gothic...),
      so Hebrew, Arabic, CJK and symbols in WPF text were boxes.

wpf-0004-system-printing-local-print-server-and-queues.patch (sg11)
    System.Printing, over winspool.drv (SgSpooler.cs, our own):
      LocalPrintServer and PrintServer (GetPrintQueue, GetPrintQueues,
      the default queue), PrintQueue (name, driver, port, print processor,
      comment, location, status and attributes and every Is... of them,
      jobs, priorities, Refresh), PrintQueueCollection,
      PrintJobInfoCollection and PrintSystemJobInfo (EnumJobs). Every
      member threw NotImplementedException -- LocalPrintServer's
      constructor too, so DYMO Connect's printer discovery stopped there
      and it found no LabelWriter. Not yet: print tickets and capabilities,
      XPS writers, AddJob, installing or deleting queues, property
      dictionaries.
